type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [454, 205, 1182, 276], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"TABLE PDO-2.\\u2014Offerings of Marketable Securities Other than Regular Weekly Treasury Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [537, 285, 1089, 311], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"[In millions of dollars. Source: Bureau of the Public Debt, Office of Financing]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 1393, 794, 1485], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Currently, all issues are sold at auction. For bill issues, the rate shown is the high bank discount rate. For note and bond issues, the rate shown is the interest rate. For details of bill offerings, see table PDO-1. As of October 1, 1997, all Treasury issues of notes and bonds are eligible for STRIPS.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1478, 550, 1504], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"2 From date of additional issue in case of a reopening.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [153, 1499, 767, 1530], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"3 In reopenings, the amount accepted is in addition to the amount of original offerings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [818, 1393, 1468, 1443], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"4 Includes securities issued to the Federal Reserve System; and to foreign and international monetary authorities, whether in exchange for maturing securities or for new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 1461, 1459, 1509], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Amounts listed as tendered and accepted are amounts tendered and awarded on auction day.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1454, 90, 1490, 134], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"39\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [373, 207, 1257, 255], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Ownership of Federal Securities\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 269, 800, 453], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Federal securities presented in the following tables are public debt securities such as savings bonds, bills, notes, and bonds that the Treasury issues. The tables also detail debt issued by other Federal agencies under special financing authorities. [See the Federal debt (FD) tables for a more complete description of the Federal debt.]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 460, 798, 676], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Effective January 1, 2001, Treasury's Bureau of the Public Debt revised formats, titles, and column headings in the \\\"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States,\\\" Table I: Summary of Treasury Securities Outstanding and Table II: Statutory Debt Limit. These changes should reduce confusion and bring the publication more in line with the public's use of terms.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 681, 800, 867], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Treasury's Financial Management Service (FMS) compiles data in the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" table OFS-1 from the \\\"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States.\\\" Effective June 2001, FMS revised procedures and categories in this table to agree with the Bureau of the Public Debt's publication changes.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 273, 1490, 460], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Table OFS-1 presents Treasury marketable and nonmarketable securities and debt issued by other Federal agencies held by Government accounts, the FRBs, and private investors. Social Security and Federal retirement trust fund investments comprise much of the Government account holdings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 467, 1490, 530], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"The FRBs acquire Treasury securities in the market as a means of executing monetary policy.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 540, 1494, 823], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Table OFS-2 presents the estimated ownership of U.S. Treasury securities. Information is primarily obtained from the Federal Reserve Board of Governors Flow of Funds data, Table L209. State, local, and foreign holdings include special issues of nonmarketable securities to municipal entities and foreign official accounts. They also include municipal, foreign official, and private holdings of marketable Treasury securities. (See footnotes to the table for description of investor categories.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1386, 1992, 1490, 2015], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"June 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 97, 180, 120], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"40\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [554, 94, 1080, 130], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"OWNERSHIP OF FEDERAL SECURITIES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [178, 189, 1454, 236], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"TABLE OFS-1.\\u2014Distribution of Federal Securities by Class of Investors and Type of Issues\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [581, 236, 1047, 269], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars. Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 273, 1488, 974], \"p