ican, Caribbean, Asian, African, and Middle East regional organizations.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1386, 1987, 1492, 2018], \"page_id\": 67}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 101, 173, 123], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"62\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [665, 99, 965, 125], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"CAPITAL MOVEMENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 302, 1352, 1539], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 1591, 1401, 1714], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"In December 2012, U.S. claims on foreigners reported by U.S. banks amounted to $3.9 trillion, a decrease of $406 billion from that recorded at yearend 2011. U.S. banking claims include holdings of foreign short-term securities but exclude holdings of foreign long-term securities. U.S. banking claims increased $257 billion in 2009 and $554 billion in 2010. However, they decreased $267 billion in 2011.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1714, 1419, 1898], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"As with U.S. banking liabilities, U.S. banking claims on foreigners are concentrated in international financial centers. Nearly 60 percent of these claims are reported opposite the United Kingdom and banking centers in the Caribbean. In the post crisis years, there has been a steady fall in claims on Caribbean banking centers, the United Kingdom, and all other Europe. In contrast, claims on Asia have consistently risen since 2008. Although the lion's share of banking claims against the U.S. is held by the international financial centers, this share has fallen while Asia's share has grown from under 5 percent in 2008 to over 15 percent in 2012.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [178, 177, 1459, 259], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"CHART CM-B.\\u2014U.S. Claims on Foreigners Reported by U.S. Banks, Brokers, and Dealers with Respect to Selected Countries\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1987, 251, 2022], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [687, 92, 984, 127], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"CAPITAL MOVEMENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1454, 92, 1494, 127], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"63\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [153, 387, 1515, 1791], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">Type of liability or claim</th><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">Calendar year</th><th colspan=\\\"5\\\">2011-2012</th></tr><tr><th></th><th></th><th>2008</th><th>2009</th><th>2010</th><th>2011 Dec.</th><th>2012 Mar.</th><th>2012 June r.</th><th>2012 Sept.</th><th>2012 Dec. p</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">Total liabilities</td><td>87,630</td><td>79,272</td><td>78,876</td><td>84,236</td><td>84,929</td><td>85,020</td><td>90,890</td><td>85,750</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">Payable in dollars</td><td>69,124</td><td>58,595</td><td>63,764</td><td>72,381</td><td>72,080</td><td>73,001</td><td>77,940</td><td>75,039</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Financial</td><td>18,650</td><td>12,986</td><td>12,225</td><td>12,651</td><td>11,746</td><td>11,893</td><td>12,994</td><td>11,966</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Short-term negotiable securities</td><td>2,740</td><td>1,300</td><td>902</td><td>936</td><td>1,430</td><td>870</td><td>545</td><td>573</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Other</td><td>15,910</td><td>11,686</td><td>11,323</td><td>11,715</td><td>10,316</td><td>11,023</td><td>12,449</td