 $1.3 billion. Stock swaps rose in 2012 to $2.8 billion. For 2013 Q1, stock swap acquisitions were zero (stock swaps data for the most recent quarter are Federal Reserve Board/Treasury estimates and are subject to substantial revisions.) These stock swaps are not reported under the TIC reporting system, but are available on the TIC Website. The TIC Website also provides estimates from the Federal Reserve Bank of New York on principal repayment flows of foreign holdings of U.S. government agency and corporate asset-backed securities (ABS). These repayments are estimated to have reduced foreign net purchases of U.S. securities by $204 billion in 2009, $231 billion in 2010, $164 billion in 2011, $226 billion in 2012, and $60 billion in the first quarter of 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [109, 1853, 1550, 1978], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"After including stock swaps and accounting for ABS repayment flows, net foreign purchases totaled $434 billion in 2009. The pace of acquisition picked up in 2010, when foreign net purchases were recorded at $668 billion. The pace of acquisitions slowed considerably in both 2011 and again in 2012, with net foreign purchases recorded at $328 billion in 2011 and $396 billion in 2012. Foreign net purchases were only $16 billion in the first quarter of 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 1989, 251, 2015], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [667, 97, 964, 127], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"CAPITAL MOVEMENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1455, 97, 1488, 127], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"79\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [330, 200, 1300, 250], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"CHART CM-D.\\u2014Net Purchases of Long-Term\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [441, 252, 1189, 302], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Foreign Securities by U.S. Investors\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [222, 337, 1410, 870], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [222, 905, 1410, 1478], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1523, 1439, 1707], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"The data on this page represent U.S. investors' purchases and sales of long-term foreign securities as reported to the TIC reporting system. U.S. investors also have acquired foreign stocks through mergers that involve stock swaps. Net acquisitions through stock swaps amounted to $7 billion in 2008, $2 billion in 2009, $12 billion in 2010, $10 billion in 2011, $15 billion in 2012, and $0.3 billion in the first quarter of 2013. (Stock swaps data for the most recent quarter are Federal Reserve Board/Treasury estimates and are subject to substantial revisions.) These stock swaps are not reported under the TIC reporting system, but are available on the TIC Website.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1711, 1439, 1869], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Including acquisitions through stock swaps, U.S. net sales of long-term foreign securities amounted to $67 billion in 2008, but U.S. investors switched to net purchases of foreign securities in 2009 with acquisitions of $185 billion. Net purchases slowed in 2010 to $103 billion but picked up slightly in 2011 to $114 billion. In 2012, U.S. investors\\u2019 net purchases slowed again to $21 billion in foreign securities. Net purchases of foreign securities picked up notably to $77 billion in the first quarter of 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1388, 1989, 1488, 2015], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 97, 173, 123], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"80\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [670, 99, 960, 125], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"CAPITAL MOVEMENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [244, 189, 1386, 280], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"SECTION V.\\u2014Holdings of, and Transactions in, Financial Derivatives Contracts with Foreigners Reported by Businesses in the United States\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [237, 297, 1395, 368], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"TABLE CM-V-1.\\u2014Gross Totals of Holdings with Positive and Negative Fair Values, by Type of Contract\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [441, 377, 1188, 405], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Holdings at end of period in millions of dollars. Source: Treasury International Capital Reporting System\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 412, 1494, 1919], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>2010</th><th>2011</th><th>2012</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr><tr><th></th><th>Dec.</th><th>Dec.</th><th>Mar. r</th><th>June r</th><th>Sept.</th><th>Dec. p</th></tr><tr><td>Gross total of holdings with negative fair values</td><td>3,541,931</td><td>4,630,539</td><td>3,865,828</td><td>4,071,326</td><td>3,846,541</td><td>3,561,985</td></tr><tr><td>Total over-the-counter (OTC) contracts</td><td>3,512,342</td><td>4,581,255</td><td>3,803,270</td><td>4,013,034</td><td>3,811,328</td><td>3,527,668</td></tr><tr><td>Single-currency interest rate contracts</td><td>2,787,529</td><td>3,799,720</td><td>3,141,181