coord\": [160, 1711, 803, 1794], \"page_id\": 105}], \"content\": \"Beginning July 1974, the International Monetary Fund adopted a technique for valuing the SDRs based on a weighted average of exchange rates for the currencies of selected member countries. The U.S. SDR holdings and allocations are valued on this basis beginning July 1974.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [847, 1711, 1474, 1836], \"page_id\": 105}], \"content\": \"Note. \\u2014 Annual balance sheets for fiscal years 1934 through 1940 appeared in the 1940 \\\"Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury\\\" and those for succeeding years appeared in subsequent reports through 1980. Quarterly balance sheets beginning with December 31, 1938, have been published in the \\\"Treasury Bulletin.\\\" Data from inception to September 30, 1978, may be found on the statements published in the January 1979 \\\"Treasury Bulletin.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1392, 1996, 1486, 2015], \"page_id\": 105}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1066, 191, 1486, 398], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"SPECIAL REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1346, 434, 1486, 471], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"Trust Funds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [721, 123, 914, 158], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1439, 97, 1494, 127], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"103\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 205, 1242, 252], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Airport and Airway Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 269, 789, 514], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"The Airport and Airway Trust Fund was established on the books of Treasury in fiscal year 1971, according to provisions of the Airport and Airway Revenue Act of 1970 [49 United States Code 1742(a), repealed]. The Tax Equity and Fiscal Responsibility Act of 1982 (Public Law 97-248, dated September 3, 1982) reestablished the trust fund in the Internal Revenue Code (26 United States Code 9502) effective September 1, 1982.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 514, 790, 759], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Treasury transfers from the general fund to the trust fund amounts equivalent to the taxes received from transportation of persons and property by air, gasoline and jet fuel used in commercial and noncommercial aircraft, and an international arrival and departure tax. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-508, dated November 5, 1990) increased rates for the excise taxes transferred to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 759, 794, 853], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Treasury bases these transfers on estimates made by the Secretary of the Treasury. These are subject to adjustments in later transfers in the amount of actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 851, 790, 981], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"The FAA Modernization and Reform Act 2012 (Public Law 112-095), effective February 14, 2012, extended the aviation excise taxes until September 30, 2015. The Act included provisions that:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 983, 790, 1228], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing passenger ticket, flight segment, and freight waybill taxes. The flight segment tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2012, the tax is $3.90. It also retained a special rule applied to flights between the continental United States and Alaska or Hawaii. This departure tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2012, the tax is $8.60.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1233, 790, 1332], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing international and departure per passenger tax. The tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2012, the tax is $17.20.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1334, 790, 1395], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing tax on payments to airlines for frequent flyer and similar awards by banks and credit\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 264, 1494, 363], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"card companies, merchants and frequent flyer program partners, such as other airlines, hotels and rental car companies, and other businesses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 368, 1490, 429], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Retained the commercial aviation fuel tax and the general aviation jet fuel/gas taxes.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [843, 436, 1494, 620], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Imposed a new surtax on fuel used in aircraft that is part of a fractional ownership program; the surtax applies to fuel used after March 31, 2012. It also changed the classification of transportation as part of a fractional ownership program from commercial aviation to noncommercial aviation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 629, 1494, 783], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Repealed the excise tax exemption for transportation by small aircraft operating on nonestablished lines. (IRS defines the term \\\"operated on an established line\\\" to mean operated with some degree of regularity between definite points).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 785, 1495, 997], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"When the provisions of 26 United States Code 9602(b) are met, amounts available in the trust fund exceed outlay requirements, Treasury invests excess amounts in public debt securities and credits the interest to the fund. Additional sums from the general fund also are credited as authorized and made available, by law, if they are needed to meet outlay requirements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 997, 1495, 1212], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Treasury makes available to the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), Department of Transportation (DOT), amounts required for outlays to carry out the Airport and Airway program. The Secretary of the Treasury makes other charges to the trust fund to transfer certain refunds of taxes and certain outfits, under section 34 of the Internal Revenue Code (IRC).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [843, 1212, 1492, 1400], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress, required by 26 U.S.C. 9602 (a), are submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Transportation. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and results of operations of the trust fund during the past fiscal year and those expected during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1382, 1989, 1494, 2018], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 101, 188, 125], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"104\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [721, 99, 913, 123], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [479, 200, 1151, 273], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-1.\\u2014Airport and Airway Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [761, 280, 867, 302], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOT]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 304, 1494, 1167], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Description</th><th>IRC section (26 United States Code)</th><th>Amount</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2011</td><td></td><td>$10,325,817,307</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes (transferred from general fund):</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Liquid fuel in a fractional ownership flight</td><td>4043</td><td>10,614,826</td></tr><tr><td>Liquid fuel other than gasoline</td><td>4041</td><td>567,236,061</td></tr><tr><td>Gasoline</td><td>4081</td><td>44,942,888</td></tr><tr><td>Transportation by airseats, berths, etc</td><td>4261 (a) (b)</td><td>8,711,445,259</td></tr><tr><td>Use of international travel facilities</td><td>4261 (c)</td><td>2,728,594,193</td></tr><tr><td>Transportation of property, cargo</td><td>4271</td><td>491,844,911</td></tr><tr><td>Gross excise taxes</td><td></td><td>12,554,678,138</td></tr><tr><td>Less refunds of taxes (reimbursed to general fund):</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Liquid fuel other than gasoline</td><td>4041</td><td>16,117,344</td></tr><tr><td>Gasoline</td><td></td><td>6,346,285</td></tr><tr><td>Total refunds of taxes</td><td></td><td>22,463,628</td></tr><tr><td>Net taxes</td><td></td><td>12,532,214,510</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td></td><td>220,627,896</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td></td><td>12,752,842,406</td></tr><tr><td>Offsetting collections</td><td></td><td>54,876,235</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Operations</td><td></td><td>5,060,694,000</td></tr><tr><td>Grants in aid</td><td></td><td>3,143,868,609</td></tr><tr><td>Facilities and equipment</td><td></td><td>2,968,584,111</td></tr><tr><td>Research, engineering, and development</td><td></td><td>187,866,172</td></tr><tr><td>Air carriers</td><td></td><td>149,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td></td><td>11,510,012,892</td></tr><tr><td>Offsetting collections</td><td></td><td>54,876,235</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2012</td><td></td><td>$11,623,523,07</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [332, 1261, 1300, 1334], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"Airport and Airway Trust Fund Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 2013-2017\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [690, 1344, 944, 1365], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars. Source: DOT)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 1367, 1495, 1768], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>2013</th><th>2014</th><th>2015</th><th>2016</th><th>2017</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>11,624</td><td>11,626</td><td>11,544</td><td>12,038</td><td>13,137</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes, net of refunds</td><td>11,921</td><td>12,199</td><td>12,648</td><td>13,209</td><td>13,804</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>232</td><td>218</td><td>201</td><td>194</td><td>238</td></tr><tr><td>$100 Surcharge</td><td></td><td>807</td><td>842</td><td>881</td><td>921</td></tr><tr><td>Offsetting collections</td><td>103</td><td>84</td><td>86</td><td>88</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>12,256</td><td>13,308</td><td>13,620</td><td>14,372</td><td>15,040</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Gross Outlays</td><td>12,254</td><td>13,390</td><td>13,126</td><td>13,273</td><td>13,301</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>11,626</td><td>11,544</td><td>12,038</td><td>13,137</td><td>14,876</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1996, 248, 2013], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [719, 94, 914, 130], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1439, 99, 1492, 127], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"105\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [472, 193, 1157, 238], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Uranium Enrichment\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [350, 238, 1280, 278], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"Decontamination and Decommissioning (D&D) Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 292, 800, 573], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"The Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal year 1993, according to provisions of the Energy Policy Act of 1992 (42 United States Code 2297g). Receipts represent (1) fees collected from domestic public utilities based on their pro rata share of purchases of separative work units from the Department of Energy (DOE) and (2) appropriations toward the Government contribution based on the balance of separative work unit purchases.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 573, 800, 816], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"Expenditures from the fund are for the purpose of (1) decontamination and decommissioning of the three gaseous diffusion plants, (2) remedial actions and related environmental restoration costs at the gaseous diffusion plants, and (3) reimbursement to uranium/thorium producers for the costs of decontamination, decommissioning, reclamation, and remedial action of uranium/thorium sites that are incident to sales to the U.S. Government.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 816, 800, 1061], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the fund exceeding current needs may be invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in obligations of the United States (1) having maturities congruent with the needs of the fund and (2) bearing interest at rates determined appropriate, taking into consideration the current average market yield on outstanding marketable obligations of the United States with remaining periods to maturity comparable to these investments.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1061, 800, 1186], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"The Secretary of the Treasury is required by 42 United States Code 2297g(b)(1) to provide an annual report to Congress, after consultation with the Secretary of Energy. This report must present the financial condition and the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 292, 1490, 358], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"results of operations of the fund during the preceding fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 358, 1492, 632], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"The Energy Policy Act of 1992 (42 United States Code 2297g-1, as amended) authorizes funding to ensure annual deposits to the fund of $518.2 million before adjustments for inflation. The Act stipulates that the Government deposit $369.6 million, adjusted for inflation, annually. The Act also calls for deposits of $150 million from domestic public utility assessments. The assessments were authorized for 15 years with the final assessment scheduled for fiscal year 2007.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 632, 1492, 816], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"Between fiscal years 1993 and 2007, the total Government contribution amount authorized by the Act was $6,281.0 million. During that time span, the Government contributed only $5,362.4 million to the fund. The resulting shortfall in authorized Government contributions was, therefore, $918.6 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 816, 1492, 1186], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"The Government continued to make annual contributions to eliminate this shortfall. Through fiscal year 2009 contributions, the overall shortfall (after adjustments for inflation) was $40.6 million. Also, during fiscal year 2009, the Government designated $390 million of American Recovery and Reinvestment Act (ARRA) funding for the fund's mission. The ARRA funding was not an actual deposit into the fund's invested balances, but it provides a dollar for dollar reduction in the required outlays from the invested balances. The DOE recognizes the ARRA funding as an offset to the Government's contribution shortfall, thereby satisfying the Government's contribution responsibility.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1386, 1985, 1492, 2018], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 92, 197, 130], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"106\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [718, 90, 916, 127], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [237, 191, 1392, 271], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-2.\\u2014Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [761, 276, 869, 302], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOE]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 311, 1492, 938], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2011</td><td>$4,968,724</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Penalties collected</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>159,238,458</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>159,238,458</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>DOE, decontamination and decommissioning activities</td><td>507,299,736</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of investments</td><td>-348,082,915</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>159,216,821</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2012</td><td>$4,990,361</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [324, 1072, 1308, 1155], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 2013-2017\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [670, 1160, 954, 1183], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"(In thousands of dollars. Source: DOE)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 1183, 1492, 1796], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>2013</th><th>2014</th><th>2015</th><th>2016</th><th>2017</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>4,990</td><td>4,990</td><td>4,990</td><td>4,990</td><td>4,990</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Interest collected</td><td>100,217</td><td>92,586</td><td>85,625</td><td>80,256</td><td>76,087</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>100,217</td><td>92,586</td><td>85,625</td><td>80,256</td><td>76,087</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>DOE, decontamination and decommissioning fund</td><td>442,493</td><td>372,732</td><td>341,193</td><td>277,372</td><td>229,151</td></tr><tr><td>Costs of investments</td><td>-342,276</td><td>-280,146</td><td>-255,568</td><td>-197,116</td><td>-153,064</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>100,217</td><td>92,586</td><td>85,625</td><td>80,256</td><td>76,087</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>4,990</td><td>4,990</td><td>4,990</td><td>4,990</td><td>4,990</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1987, 248, 2018], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [721, 94, 914, 127], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1439, 97, 1492, 130], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"107\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [364, 191, 1264, 240], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Black Lung Disability Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 252, 800, 436], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Black Lung Disability Trust Fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal year 1978 according to the Black Lung Benefits Revenue Act of 1977 (Public Law 95-227). The Black Lung Benefits Revenue Act of 1981 (Public Law 97-119) reestablished the fund in the Internal Revenue Code (IRC), 26 United States Code 9501.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 436, 798, 773], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1985 (Public Law 99-272), enacted April 7, 1986, provided for an increase in the coal tax rates effective April 1, 1986, through December 31, 1995, and a 5-year forgiveness of interest retroactive to October 1, 1985. The 5-year moratorium on interest payments ended on September 30, 1990. Payment of interest on advances resumed in fiscal year 1991. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1987 (Public Law 100-203, title X, section 10503), signed December 22, 1987, extended the temporary increase in the coal tax through December 31, 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 773, 798, 1204], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Emergency Economic Stabilization Act of 2008 (Public Law 110-343, title I, subtitle B, section 113), enacted October 3, 2008, restructured the Trust Fund Debt by 1) refinancing the outstanding principal of the repayable advances and unpaid interest on such advances and 2) providing a one time Appropriation to the Trust Fund in an amount sufficient to pay to the general fund of the Treasury the difference between the market value of the outstanding repayable advances, plus accrued interest and the proceeds from the obligations issued by the Trust Fund to the Secretary of the Treasury. The Act also extends the temporary increase in the coal tax through December 31, 2018, and allows the prepayment of the Trust Fund debt prior to the maturity date.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 252, 1492, 467], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Code designates the following receipts to be appropriated and transferred from the general fund of the Treasury to the trust fund: excise taxes on coal sold; taxable expenditures of self-dealing by, and excess contributions to, private black lung benefit trusts; reimbursements by responsible mine operators; and related fines, penalties and interest charges.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 467, 1490, 589], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"Estimates made by the Secretary of the Treasury determine monthly transfers of amounts for excise taxes to the trust fund subject to adjustments in later transfers to actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 589, 1494, 804], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"After retirement of the current indebtedness, amounts available in the fund exceeding current expenditure requirements will be invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in interest-bearing public debt securities. Any interest earned will be credited to the fund. Also credited, if necessary, will be repayable advances from the general fund to meet outlay requirements exceeding available revenues.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 806, 1492, 957], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"To carry out the program, amounts are made available to the Department of Labor (DOL). Also charged to the fund are administrative expenses incurred by the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) and the Treasury, repayments of advances from the general fund and interest on advances.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 957, 1495, 1174], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Code requires the Secretary of the Treasury to submit an annual report to Congress after consultation with the Secretary of Labor and the Secretary of HHS [26 United States Code 9602(a)]. The report must present the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and the expected condition and operations of the fund during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1386, 1989, 1492, 2018], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 90, 202, 137], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"108\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [701, 82, 934, 132], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [468, 182, 1168, 269], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-3.\\u2014Black Lung Disability Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [752, 273, 872, 306], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOL]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 306, 1504, 1068], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2011</td><td>$50,028,790</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes (transferred from general fund):</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>$1.10 tax on underground coal</td><td>292,564,600</td></tr><tr><td>$0.55 tax on surface coal</td><td>228,177,065</td></tr><tr><td>4.4 percent tax on underground coal</td><td>9,861,333</td></tr><tr><td>4.4 percent tax on surface coal</td><td>98,498,420</td></tr><tr><td>Fines, penalties, and interest</td><td>881,508</td></tr><tr><td>Collection\\u2014responsible mine operators</td><td>11,618,228</td></tr><tr><td>Recovery of prior year funds</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Repayable advances from the general fund</td><td>214,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>855,601,154</td></tr><tr><td>Net receipts</td><td>855,601,154</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Treasury administrative expenses</td><td>555,726</td></tr><tr><td>Salaries and expenses\\u2014DOL\\u2014Departmental Management</td><td>25,217,000</td></tr><tr><td>Salaries and expenses\\u2014DOL\\u2014Office of Inspector General</td><td>327,000</td></tr><tr><td>Salaries and expenses\\u2014DOL\\u