. Court of Federal Claims expenses</td><td>5,004</td><td>5,004</td><td>5,004</td><td>5,004</td><td>5,004</td></tr><tr><td>U.S. Department of Justice expenses</td><td>13,732</td><td>13,732</td><td>13,732</td><td>13,732</td><td>13,732</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>18,736</td><td>18,736</td><td>18,736</td><td>18,736</td><td>18,736</td></tr><tr><td>Nonexpenditure transfers:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Transfers to health resources</td><td>197,484</td><td>203,409</td><td>209,511</td><td>215,796</td><td>222,270</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays/transfers</td><td>216,220</td><td>222,145</td><td>228,247</td><td>234,532</td><td>241,046</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>3,575,867</td><td>3,864,277</td><td>3,796,503</td><td>3,912,658</td><td>4,032,819</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1989, 244, 2015], \"page_id\": 130}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [718, 94, 914, 127], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1443, 99, 1492, 125], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"127\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [393, 212, 1239, 290], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Wool Research, Development, and Promotion Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 314, 805, 738], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"The Wool Research, Development, and Promotion Trust Fund was established in fiscal year 2000 with a sunset provision effective January, 1, 2004, according to provisions of the Trade and Development Act of 2000 (Public Law 106-200, signed May 18, 2000). The Trade Act of 2002 (Public Law 107-210, signed August 6, 2002) extended the sunset provision to January 1, 2006. The Miscellaneous Trade and Technical Corrections Act of 2004 (Public Law 108-429, signed December 3, 2004) extended the sunset provision to 2008. The Pension Protection Act of 2006 (Public Law 109-280, signed August 17, 2006) extended the sunset provision to 2010. The Emergency Economic Stabilization Act of 2008 (Public Law 110-343, signed October 3, 2008) extended the sunset provision to 2015.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 742, 800, 891], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"The Act provides that the Secretary of the Treasury shall transfer to the trust fund out of the general fund of the U.S. Treasury amounts determined to be equivalent to the duty received on articles under chapters 51 and 52 of the Harmonized Tariff Schedule of the United States.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 309, 1490, 495], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"amount to be transferred is limited to $2,500,000 in any fiscal year and may be invested in U.S. Treasury securities. The Secretary of Agriculture is authorized to provide grants to a nationally recognized council established for the development of the United States wool market for the following purposes:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 502, 1490, 594], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"Assist United States wool producers in improving the quality of wool and wool production methods for wool produced in the United States.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 601, 1492, 665], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"Disseminate information on improvements to United States wool producers.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 672, 1490, 733], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"Assist United States wool producers in developing and promoting the wool market.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 733, 1492, 858], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress are required on the financial condition and the results of the operations of the trust fund during the past fiscal year and on its expected condition and operations during the next fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [304, 940, 1335, 1018], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-14.\\u2014Wool Research, Development, and Promotion Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1042, 1490, 1353], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">(In thousands of dollars. Source: Department of Agriculture)</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2011</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Harmonized tariff</td><td>2,250</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>2,250</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Expenditure</td><td>2,250</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>2,250</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2012</td><td>-</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [377, 1402, 1262, 1476], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"Wool Research, Development, and Promotion Trust Fund\\nExpected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [607, 1492, 1035, 1513], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"(In thousands of dollars. Source: Department of Agriculture)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1532, 1490, 1857], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Harmonized tariff</td><td>2,250</td></tr><tr><td>Sequestration</td><td>115</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>2,135</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Expenditure</td><td>2,135</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>2,135</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>-</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1386, 1992, 1494, 2018], \"page_id\": 131}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 99, 193, 127], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"128\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [721, 97, 914, 127], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [321, 196, 1306, 238], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Agriculture Disaster Relief Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 250, 801, 375], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"The Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008 (Public Law 110-246) created the \\\"Agriculture Disaster Relief Trust Fund\\\" (Disaster Trust Fund). The Disaster Trust Fund is described in Section 902 of the public law.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 375, 801, 684], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"The Disaster Trust Fund is appropriated an amount equivalent to 3.08 percent of the amounts received in the general fund of the Treasury of the United States during fiscal years 2008 through 2011 attributable to the duties collected on articles entered, or withdrawn from the warehouse, for consumption under the Harmonized Tariff Schedule of the United States. The collection activity is made by the U.S. Department of Homeland Security, U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP). The CBP transfers the funds monthly to the Disaster Trust Fund Receipt Account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 684, 801, 865], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"The Disaster Trust Fund shall make amounts available for the purpose of expenditures to meet obligations of the United States incurred under Section 901 of the Trade Act of 1974 and Section 531 of the Federal Crop Insurance Act. The Disaster Trust Fund will be used to make payments to farmers and ranchers under five disaster programs.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [178, 872, 798, 933], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"Supplemental Revenue Assistance Payments Program (SURE)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [177, 938, 685, 974], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"Livestock Forage Disaster Program (LFP)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [869, 259, 1308, 290], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"Livestock Indemnity Program (LIP)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [869, 299, 1268, 330], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"Tree Assistance Program (TAP)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [869, 337, 1488, 396], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"Emergency Assistance for Livestock, Honey Bees, and Farm-Raised Fish Program (ELAP)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 398, 1490, 519], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"The Farm Service Agency shall invest such portions of the Disaster Trust Fund that is not required to meet current payment amounts. Investments may only be made in interest bearing obligations of the United States.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 519, 1490, 764], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"The American Recovery and Reinvestment Act (ARRA) of 2009 (Public Law 111-5) created the \\\"Agriculture Disaster Relief Trust Fund, Recovery Act\\\" (Disaster Trust Fund-Recovery Act). The Disaster Trust Fund-Recovery Act provided for additional payments to farmers and ranchers from the SURE and TAP programs. The additional payments are tracked separately to meet the ARRA reporting requirements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 764, 1488, 825], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"The Disaster Trust Fund has indefinite borrowing authority via repayable advances.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 825, 1490, 981], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress, required by 19 United States Code 2497(a), are submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and those expected during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [430, 1032, 1209, 1106], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-15.\\u2014Agriculture Disaster Relief Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [601, 1120, 1031, 1143], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"[In thousands of dollars. Source: Department of Agriculture]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 1157, 1490, 1803], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Cumulative debt, start of year</td><td>696,041</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>516,821</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Transferred from customers</td><td>36</td></tr><tr><td>Borrowing authority</td><td>400,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>400,036</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Supplemental Revenue Assistance Payments Program</td><td>566,967</td></tr><tr><td>Livestock