cluding loans associated with repurchase agreements, and non-negotiable short-term securities.\\n3 Foreign currency data are as of the previous quarter-end.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 1766, 1484, 1881], \"page_id\": 62}], \"content\": \"4 As of January 2008, includes Austria, Belgium, Cyprus, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, Malta, the Netherlands, Portugal, Slovenia, and Spain. For data as of January 2009, also includes Slovakia. For data as of January 2011, also includes Estonia.\\n5 Includes European, Latin American, Caribbean, Asian, African, and Middle East regional organizations.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1388, 1994, 1488, 2013], \"page_id\": 62}], \"content\": \"June 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 101, 175, 123], \"page_id\": 63}], \"content\": \"58\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [667, 94, 967, 123], \"page_id\": 63}], \"content\": \"CAPITAL MOVEMENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [164, 205, 1470, 288], \"page_id\": 63}], \"content\": \"CHART CM-A.\\u2014U.S. Liabilities to Foreigners Reported by U.S. Banks, Brokers, and Dealers with Respect to Selected Countries\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [259, 351, 1346, 940], \"page_id\": 63}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [286, 999, 1341, 1542], \"page_id\": 63}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [224, 1598, 1395, 1902], \"page_id\": 63}], \"content\": \"U.S. liabilities to foreigners reported by U.S. banks were recorded at $4.7 trillion in March 2012, a decrease of $166 billion from yearend 2011. U.S. banking liabilities include foreign holdings of U.S. short-term securities but exclude foreign holdings of U.S. long-term securities. U.S. banking liabilities decreased about $427 billion in 2009 but increased about $117 billion in 2010 and $293 billion in 2011. U.S. banking liabilities are concentrated in international financial centers. The data on this page show that nearly 60 percent of U.S. banking liabilities is currently recorded against the United Kingdom and banking centers in the Caribbean. These financial centers, particularly the United Kingdom, recorded much of the decline in banking liabilities during the financial crisis and much of the rebound in 2010. In 2011, liabilities to all of Europe grew rapidly as European banks provided funds to support their U.S. branches. However, liabilities to Europe declined in the first quarter of 2012, as did liabilities to all regions, except Asia.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1992, 250, 2013], \"page_id\": 63}], \"content\": \"June 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [659, 92, 971, 130], \"page_id\": 64}], \"content\": \"CAPITAL MOVEMENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1450, 97, 1492, 130], \"page_id\": 64}], \"content\": \"59\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 189, 1439, 243], \"page_id\": 64}], \"content\": \"SECTION II.\\u2014Claims on Foreigners Reported by Banks in the United States\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [528, 252, 1102, 288], \"page_id\": 64}], \"content\": \"TABLE CM-II-1.\\u2014Total Claims by Type\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [444, 297, 1184, 328], \"page_id\": 64}], \"content\": \"[Position at end of period in millions of dollars. Source: Treasury