6 [Public Law 99-499, dated October 17, 1986 (26 United States Code 9507)].\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 578, 800, 639], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"The authority to collect excise taxes on petroleum and chemicals, and an environmental tax for all corporations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 269, 1495, 422], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"with modified alternative taxable income in excess of $2 million, expired in 1995. To implement the Superfund program, amounts are appropriated from the Superfund to the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) for programmatic and administrative expenses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 431, 1488, 613], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of Treasury is required by 26 United States Code 9602(a). These reports present the financial condition of the Superfund and the results of operation for the past fiscal year, and its expected condition during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [461, 688, 1175, 764], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-5.\\u2014Hazardous Substance Superfund 1,2 Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [767, 773, 872, 797], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"[Source: EPA]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 797, 1490, 1768], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2011</td><td>$138,600,000</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Crude and petroleum</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Certain chemicals</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Corporate environmental</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>General fund appropriation</td><td>1,075,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Cost re