ge_id\": 122}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>2013</th><th>2014</th><th>2015</th><th>2016</th><th>2017</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>1,157</td><td>1,259</td><td>1,362</td><td>1,477</td><td>1,606</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Taxes<sup>2</sup></td><td>181</td><td>180</td><td>181</td><td>182</td><td>182</td></tr><tr><td>Interest</td><td>20</td><td>27</td><td>38</td><td>51</td><td>64</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>201</td><td>207</td><td>219</td><td>233</td><td>246</td></tr><tr><td>Appropriations</td><td>99</td><td>104</td><td>104</td><td>104</td><td>104</td></tr><tr><td>Other Expenses</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>1,259</td><td>1,362</td><td>1,477</td><td>1,606</td><td>1,748</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [153, 1888, 790, 1971], \"page_id\": 122}], \"content\": \"1 Reporting in this trust fund table is consistent with previously reported presentations. However, the structure of this table may not accurately reflect the status of the trust fund. As a result, this table may be revised in future reports and other resources should be utilized for accurate trust fund reporting.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [827, 1888, 1443, 1966], \"page_id\": 122}], \"content\": \"2 Taxes are estimated.\\n3 In fiscal year 2013, a total of 104 million is enacted. Of this amount, $5 million was sequestered and retained in the trust fund. Sequestrable amounts of future funds are unknown at this time.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1987, 253, 2013], \"page_id\": 122}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [718, 97, 916, 127], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1435, 94, 1494, 130], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"119\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [472, 191, 1157, 233], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Nuclear Waste Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 252, 805, 500], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"The Nuclear Waste Fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal year 1983, according to section 302 of the Nuclear Waste Policy Act of 1982 [Public Law 97-425, codified at 42 United States Code 10222I]. Receipts represent fees collected from public utilities based on electricity generated by nuclear power reactors and spent nuclear fuel. Expenditures from the fund are for purposes of radioactive waste disposal activities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 502, 805, 653], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the fund exceeding current needs may be invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in obligations of the United States (1) having maturities in tandem with the needs of the waste fund and (2) bearing interest at rates determined appropriate, taking into\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [827, 250, 1494, 441], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"consideration the current average market yield on outstanding marketable obligations of the United States with remaining periods to maturity comparable to the maturities of such investments, except that the interest rate on such investments shall not exceed the average interest rate applicable to existing borrowings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 436, 1494, 622], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of the Department of Energy (DOE), is required by 42 United States Code 10222(e)(1). This report must present the financial condition and the results of operations of the waste fund during the preceding fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 700, 1100, 785], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-9.\\u2014Nuclear Waste Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [765, 787, 883, 816], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOE]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 816, 1501, 1608], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2011</td><td>$2,132,589</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td>753,147,270</td></tr><tr><td>Penalties and interest on fee payments</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>1,584,114,979</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>2,337,262,249</td></tr><tr><td>Nonexpenditure transfers:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>SF-1151 transfers in (+)</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>SF-1151 transfers out (-)</td><td>-3,400,000</td></tr><tr><td>Net nonexpenditure transfers</td><td>-3,400,000</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>DOE radioactive waste disposal activities</td><td>9,543,521</td></tr><tr><td>Cost investments</td><td>2,324,553,909</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>2,334,097,430</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2012</td><td>$1,897,408</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1377, 1985, 1499, 2018], \"page_id\": 123}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 94, 195, 125], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"120\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [716, 94, 918, 125], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [355, 196, 1277, 243], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"CHARTS TF-A and B.\\u2014Major Trust Funds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [401, 243, 1270, 297], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"[Data depicted in these charts are derived from the Trust Fund tables, which are provided by various Government agencies. See tables TF-1, TF-3, TF-5, TF-6 and TF-9.]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [230, 384, 1346, 945], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [240, 1183, 512, 1426], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"Receipts and Expenses, Fiscal Year 2012 (In billions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [596, 1106, 1433, 1806], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1989, 251, 2015], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [719, 97, 914, 127], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1439, 92, 1490, 125], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"121\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [435, 196, 1197, 236], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Reforestation Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 250, 800, 434], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"The Reforestation Trust Fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal year 1981 to continue through September 30, 1985, according to provisions of Title III\\u2014Reforestation, of the Recreational Boating Safety and Facilities Improvement Act of 1980 [Public Law 96-451, codified at 16 United States Code 1606a(a)].\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 438, 801, 776], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"The act provides that the Secretary of the Treasury shall transfer to the trust fund tariffs, limited to not more than $30 million for any fiscal year, received in the Treasury from October 1, 1979, through September 30, 1985, on (1) rough and primary wood products and wood waste; (2) lumber, flooring and moldings; and (3) wood veneers, plywood, other wood-veneer assemblies and building boards. Public Law 99-190, title II, 99 Statutes at Large 1245, extended the receipts for the trust fund. Amounts available in the reforestation trust fund exceeding current withdrawals are invested in interest-bearing obligations of the United States\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 250, 1494, 370], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"or in obligations guaranteed as to both principal and interest by the United States. The interest on, and the proceeds from the sale or redemption of, any obligations are credited to the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 372, 1494, 526], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"The Secretary of the Department of Agriculture is authorized to obligate available sums in the trust fund (including any amounts not obligated in previous years) for (1) reforestation and timber stand improvement and (2) administrative costs of the Government for these activities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 526, 1495, 712], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"Annual reports are required by 16 United States Code 1606aI (1) to be submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Agriculture, on the financial condition and the results of the operations of the trust fund during the past fiscal year and on its expected condition and operations during the next fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [523, 825, 1117, 900], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-10.\\u2014Reforestation Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [692, 908, 949, 933], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"[Source: Department of Agriculture]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 945, 1492, 1332], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2011<sup>1</sup></td><td>$4,853,947</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes (tariffs)</td><td>30,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Redemption of investment</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>30,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Expenditure</td><td>28,688,953</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>28,688,953</td></tr><tr><td>Adjustment</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2012</td><td>$6,164,994</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [153, 1346, 572, 1372], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"1The beginning balance for fiscal year 2011 was adjusted.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [375, 1419, 1264, 1494], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"Reforestation Trust Fund\\nExpected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [607, 1504, 1035, 1530], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"[In thousands of dollars. Source: Department of Agriculture]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [153, 1542, 1488, 1794], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>6,165</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes (tariffs)</td><td>30,000</td></tr><tr><td>Redemption of investment</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>30,000</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays</td><td>30,000</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>6,165</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1388, 1989, 1494, 2018], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 94, 193, 127], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"122\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [714, 94, 916, 130], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [239, 207, 1390, 255], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Sport Fish Restoration and Boating Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 276, 800, 644], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"The Aquatic Resources Trust Fund (ARTF) was established on the books of the Treasury pursuant to the Deficit Reduction Act of 1984 [Public Law 98-369, division A, title X, section 1016(a), approved July 18, 1984]. The ARTF was restructured and renamed the Sport Fish Restoration and Boating Trust Fund by the Safe, Accountable, Flexible, Efficient Transportation Equity Act: A Legacy for Users or \\\"SAFETEA-LU\\\" [Public Law 109-59, title XI, subtitle B, part 2, section 11115, approved August 10, 2005,] as amended by the Sportfishing and Recreational Boating Safety Amendments Act of 2005 [Public Law 109-74, approved September 29, 2005].\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 644, 801, 1136], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"Section 3 of the Dingell-Johnson Sport Fish Restoration Act, 16 United States Code 777, provides authorization of appropriations to the states to carry out the provisions of the act, and Section 4 provides the division of the remaining annual appropriation not authorized in Section 3. SAFETEA-LU comprehensively amended Section 3 and reauthorized the Sport Fish Restoration Program (for fiscal years 2006-2009) to permanently appropriate boating safety funds; to modify distribution of funds whereby all accounts receive a fixed percentage of the total fund annually; and to modify the excise tax on certain sport fishing equipment. From October 1, 2010, through June 30, 2012, the authority for SAFETEA-LU was extended via several public laws. In June 2012, Public Law 112-141, Moving Ahead for Progress in the 21st Century Act (MAP-21), established new authority for Section 4 through September 30, 2014.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 276, 1494, 585], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"Effective October 1, 2005, motorboat fuel taxes (less $1 million transferred to the Land and Water Conservation Fund) and small engine gasoline taxes [pursuant to the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990, Public Law 101-508, title XI, section 11211(i) (2) and (3)] were transferred from the Highway Trust Fund to the Sport Fish Restoration and Boating Trust Fund. In addition, amounts equivalent to the excise taxes received on sport fishing equipment and import duties on fishing tackle, yachts, and pleasure craft are appropriated into the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 582, 1494, 797], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"Amounts in the trust fund are used, as provided by appropriation acts, for the purposes of carrying out the Dingell-Johnson Sport Fish Restoration Act, approved August 9, 1950; Section 7404(d) of the Transportation Equity Act for the 21st Century; and the Coastal Wetlands Planning, Protection and Restoration Act (each as in effect on the date of enactment of the MAP-21).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 797, 1494, 922], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"The general provisions of 26 United States Code 9602(b) are responsible for making amounts available in the fund exceeding outlay requirements to be invested in public debt securities with the interest credited to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 922, 1494, 1075], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"As required by 26 United States Code 9602(a), annual reports to Congress must be submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury. These reports will cover the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and those expected during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1989, 246, 2018], \"page_id\": 126}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [719, 97, 911, 127], \"page_id\": 127}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1437, 92, 1494, 130], \"page_id\": 127}], \"content\": \"123\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [375, 226, 1275, 302], \"page_id\": 127}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-11.\\u2014Sport Fish Restoration and Boating Trust Fund Sport Fish Restoration Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [696, 304, 949, 335], \"page_id\": 127}], \"content\": \"(Source: Bureau of the Public Debt)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [157, 346, 1492, 1065], \"page_id\": 127}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balanc