Lung Benefits Revenue Act of 1977 (Public Law 95-227). The Black Lung Benefits Revenue Act of 1981 (Public Law 97-119) reestablished the fund in the Internal Revenue Code (IRC), 26 United States Code 9501.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 436, 798, 773], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1985 (Public Law 99-272), enacted April 7, 1986, provided for an increase in the coal tax rates effective April 1, 1986, through December 31, 1995, and a 5-year forgiveness of interest retroactive to October 1, 1985. The 5-year moratorium on interest payments ended on September 30, 1990. Payment of interest on advances resumed in fiscal year 1991. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1987 (Public Law 100-203, title X, section 10503), signed December 22, 1987, extended the temporary increase in the coal tax through December 31, 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 773, 798, 1204], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Emergency Economic Stabilization Act of 2008 (Public Law 110-343, title I, subtitle B, section 113), enacted October 3, 2008, restructured the Trust Fund Debt by 1) refinancing the outstanding principal of the repayable advances and unpaid interest on such advances and 2) providing a one time Appropriation to the Trust Fund in an amount sufficient to pay to the general fund of the Treasury the difference between the market value of the outstanding repayable advances, plus accrued interest and the proceeds from the obligations issued by the Trust Fund to the Secretary of the Treasury. The Act also extends the temporary increase in the coal tax through December 31, 2018, and allows the prepayment of the Trust Fund debt prior to the maturity date.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 252, 1492, 467], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Code designates the following receipts to be appropriated and transferred from the general fund of the Treasury to the trust fund: excise taxes on coal sold; taxable expenditures of self-dealing by, and excess contributions to, private black lung benefit trusts; reimbursements by responsible mine operators; and related fines, penalties and interest charges.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 467, 1490, 589], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"Estimates made by the Secretary of the Treasury determine monthly transfers of amounts for excise taxes to the trust fund subject to adjustments in later transfers to actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 589, 1494, 804], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"After retirement of the current indebtedness, amounts available in the fund exceeding current expenditure requirements will be invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in interest-bearing public debt securities. Any interest earned will be credited to the fund. Also credited, if necessary, will be repayable advances from the general fund to meet outlay requirements exceeding available revenues.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 806, 1492, 957], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"To carry out the program, amounts are made available to the Department of Labor (DOL). Also charged to the fund are administrative expenses incurred by the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) and the Treasury, repayments of advances from the general fund and interest on advances.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 957, 1495, 1174], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Code requires the Secretary of the Treasury to submit an annual report to Congress after consultation with the Secretary of Labor and the Secretary of HHS [26 United States Code 9602(a)]. The report must present the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and the expected condition and operations of the fund during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1386, 1989, 1492, 2018], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"June 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 90, 202, 137], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"108\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [701, 82, 934, 132], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [468, 182, 1168, 269], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-3.\\u2014Black Lung Disability Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2012\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [752, 273, 872, 306], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOL]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 306, 1504, 1068], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2011</td><td>$50,028,790</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes (transferred from general fund):</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>$1.10 tax on underground coal</td><td>292,564,600</td></tr><tr><td>$0.55 tax on surface coal</td><td>228,177,065</td></tr><tr><td>4.4 percent tax on underground coal</td><td>9,861,333</td></tr><tr><td>4.4 percent tax on surface coal</td><td>98,498,420</td></tr><tr><td>Fines, penalties, and interest</td><td>881,508</td></tr><tr><td>Collection\\u2014responsible mine operators</td><td>11,618,228</td></tr><tr><td>Recovery of prior year funds</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Repayable advances from the general fund</td><td>214,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>855,601,154</td></tr><tr><td>Net receipts</td><td>855,601,154</td></tr>